WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.206
Alex has just bought a house.

2
00:00:02.206 --> 00:00:11.165
Now six organisations need the new address: the state, the county, the bank, the insurer, the employer's payroll, and the mortgage servicer.

3
00:00:12.014 --> 00:00:16.847
Usually that is six forms, and six copies of an address that slowly drift apart.

4
00:00:17.697 --> 00:00:19.945
In Alex's pod there is one address.

5
00:00:19.945 --> 00:00:27.650
It is described the way a data team would describe a data product: one owner, a stated purpose, and a list of consumers.

6
00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:29.791
Alex changes it once.

7
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:34.275
The proof of address is already in the pod: the deed recorded at closing.

8
00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:37.033
Then Alex chooses who should know.

9
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:43.894
Six standing grants, all to the same record, each for one purpose: keeping the address current.

10
00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:48.041
The state's driver services reads the address and its evidence.

11
00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:52.261
It issues a new licence credential, and withdraws the old one.

12
00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.715
The county treasurer reads it, so tax bills go to the right house.

13
00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:01.665
The insurer reads it, and the car policy follows Alex to the new address.

14
00:01:02.515 --> 00:01:07.280
The bank, the payroll provider and the servicer read the same record.

15
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.490
Six readers, one copy, no forms.

16
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.284
Alex is closing the old bank account, so the bank no longer needs to know.

17
00:01:15.134 --> 00:01:16.597
Its grant is withdrawn.

18
00:01:19.526 --> 00:01:22.231
A week later Alex corrects the unit number.

19
00:01:22.231 --> 00:01:24.873
Five organisations pick up the correction.

20
00:01:24.873 --> 00:01:27.075
The bank asks, and the pod refuses.

21
00:01:27.925 --> 00:01:31.053
The bank's copy is now out of date, and it knows it is.

22
00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:34.978
That is the difference between holding a copy and reading the source.

23
00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:36.512
One record.

24
00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:37.629
Six organisations.

25
00:01:37.629 --> 00:01:38.437
Eleven reads.

26
00:01:38.437 --> 00:01:42.411
Every one of them is listed here with the grant that allowed it.

27
00:01:43.261 --> 00:01:46.495
This is the same pod that carried Alex's mortgage.

28
00:01:46.495 --> 00:01:51.411
To build the next sector with us, join the EDMA Solid Community of Practice.
